{title: Herre, du har vært vår bolig}
{subtitle: Psalm 90}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 78}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Lord, you have been our dwelling place
Through [Eb]every age and [Bb]year
Be[Gm7]fore the mountains came to birth
You are [Eb]God, [F7]and you are [Bb]here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You turn us back to [Gm]dust again
You [Eb]say, Return, and [Bb]so we go
A thousand years are [Gm]in your sight
Like [Eb]yesterday, gone [F7]long a[Bb]go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
At [Gm]morning grass is [Eb]fresh and green
By [Bb]evening it is dry and [F]gone
So [Gm]teach us, Lord, to [Eb]count our days
And give us hearts of [F]wisdom
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Lord, you have [Bb]been our dwelling [Gm]place
Through every [Eb]age and year
Be[Bb]fore the mountains came to [Gm]birth
You are [Eb]God, and [F]you are [Bb]here
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro}
| [Bb] | [Gm] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
